---
import '../styles/global.css';
import { aliasElbow } from '../lib/layout.ts';
const previewCurve = aliasElbow({ x: 236, y: 200 }, { x: 50, y: 112 }, 150, 52);
---
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="Build clear flow diagrams, explore boolean branches, and simulate every what-if. Automatic layout, loop references, and browser-local saving." />
    <title>Show the Path — Make your thinking visible</title>
  </head>
  <body class="landing">
    <nav class="landing-nav" aria-label="Main navigation"><a class="brand" href="/"><span class="brand-mark">↳</span> show the path</a><div class="landing-nav-links"><a href="#features">Features</a><a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a><a class="primary" href="/builder">Open builder ↗</a></div></nav>
    <main>
      <section class="landing-hero">
        <div class="hero-copy"><span class="hero-pill"><span class="status-dot"></span> A calmer way to map what happens next</span><h1>Big ideas.<br />Clear paths.<br /><em>One step at a time.</em></h1><p>Turn the flow in your head into something you can see. Build the happy path, branch into the what-ifs, and walk through every possibility.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="primary" href="/builder">Start mapping your idea →</a><a href="#how-it-works">See how it works ↓</a></div><div class="hero-footnote"><span>✓ No account needed</span><span>✓ Saved in your browser</span><span>✓ Desktop-first</span></div></div>
        <div class="hero-diagram" aria-label="Example flow with a loop reference">
          <div class="preview-topbar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>A little launch plan</span></div>
          <div class="preview-diagram">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 480 366" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <defs><marker id="preview-loop-arrow" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="7" refY="4" orient="auto"><path d="M1,1 L7,4 L1,7" fill="none" stroke="#36744e" stroke-width="1.5" /></marker></defs>
              <path d="M125 76V112 M125 164V200 M125 252V288 M200 226H236" stroke="#b7c8a6" stroke-width="1.5" />
              <path d="m121 106 4 6 4-6m-8 82 4 6 4-6m-8 82 4 6 4-6m103-66 6 4-6 4" stroke="#a5bc8e" />
              <path class="preview-loop-curve" d={previewCurve} stroke="#36744e" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#preview-loop-arrow)" />
            </svg>
            <div class="preview-node preview-start"><small>● ENTRY POINT</small>Start</div>
            <div id="preview-origin" class="preview-node preview-step" tabindex="-1"><small class="preview-kind">STEP</small>Shape your idea</div>
            <div class="preview-node preview-decision"><span class="decision-icon" aria-hidden="true">◆</span><small class="preview-kind">DECISION</small><span>Ready to build?</span></div>
            <span class="preview-label yes">Yes</span><span class="preview-label no">No</span>
            <div class="preview-node preview-finish">Build something small</div>
            <div class="preview-alias-group">
              <button class="preview-node preview-alternative" aria-label="Preview loop to Shape your idea"><small>↩ LOOP TO</small>Shape your idea</button>
              <a class="preview-jump" href="#preview-origin" aria-label="Go to preview origin" title="Go to referred step">↗</a>
            </div>
            <span class="preview-tip">Loop references always point home ↗</span>
          </div>
          <div class="preview-badge">✧ Automatically arranged. Always clear.</div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <div class="landing-strip"><span>↓ Follow the happy path</span><span>◇ Make room for the what-ifs</span><span>↩ Loop back, without the clutter</span><span>▷ Think it through in simulation</span></div>
      <section class="features-section" id="features"><div class="section-heading"><div class="eyebrow">LESS ARRANGING. MORE THINKING.</div><h2>Everything flows from here.</h2><p>No wrestling with arrows or nudging boxes into place.<br />Just your idea, and the next right step.</p></div><div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-icon">↓</span><h3>A happy path that stays happy.</h3><p>Click to add a step. Your flow grows vertically, with automatic layout keeping the main path in one clean column.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-icon">◆</span><h3>Simple questions. Clear branches.</h3><p>Every decision asks a boolean question. Yes goes down. No goes right. More alternatives? Add another decision.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-icon">↩</span><h3>Come full circle.</h3><p>Loop to an existing step by name. Its translucent alias draws every path it closes, and the arrow jumps straight to the original.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-icon">▷</span><h3>Take your idea for a walk.</h3><p>Switch to simulation, choose an outcome, and follow the path. Go back, restart, and explore a different possibility.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-icon">⌘</span><h3>A home for every flow.</h3><p>Create, rename, and duplicate multiple flows. Changes save to IndexedDB in this browser—no account or backend required.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-icon">⊞</span><h3>Never lose the bigger picture.</h3><p>When a flow grows beyond the canvas, a clickable minimap helps you find your way. Undo and redo keep edits forgiving.</p></article>
      </div></section>
      <section class="how-section" id="how-it-works"><div class="section-heading"><div class="eyebrow">FROM IN YOUR HEAD TO IN FRONT OF YOU</div><h2>Three steps to a clearer picture.</h2></div><div class="how-grid"><article><span>01 / BUILD</span><h3>Start with the next step.</h3><p>Name your flow and add a few steps. Give each one a title and as much context as it needs.</p></article><article><span>02 / BRANCH</span><h3>Ask “what if?”</h3><p>Add a diamond when the path splits. Explore the alternative to the right, or loop to somewhere familiar.</p></article><article><span>03 / SIMULATE</span><h3>Follow your own thinking.</h3><p>Walk from Start through each choice. Find the gaps and refine the flow before taking it into the real world.</p></article></div></section>
      <section class="landing-cta"><div class="eyebrow">GIVE THAT IDEA SOMEWHERE TO GO</div><h2>Your next clear path starts here.</h2><p>A blank canvas. A first step. A little more clarity.</p><a class="primary" href="/builder">Open the builder →</a><small>POC · Desktop editing · Flows stay in this browser. Clearing site data removes saved flows, so don’t use this version as the only copy of important work.</small></section>
      <p class="roadmap-note">On the horizon: accounts, backend saving, sharing, and export to PDF, Mermaid, and Markdown.<br />Not part of this POC—just a look at where the path leads next.</p>
    </main>
    <footer class="landing-footer"><a class="brand" href="/"><span class="brand-mark">↳</span> show the path</a><span>For ideas that deserve a little clarity.</span></footer>
  </body>
</html>
